    "summary": "**Root cause:** The `ad` Service was missing from the `astronomy-shop` namespace. The `ad` Deployment and its pod were running fine, but the frontend's `AD_ADDR` is `ad:8080`, so the frontend could not resolve the name. That produced the `Name resolution failed for target dns:ad:8080` errors. I found no event showing who deleted the Service, so I can't say how it went missing.\n\n**Fix:** I recreated the `ad` ClusterIP Service on port 8080 (targetPort 8080, selector `opentelemetry.io/name: ad`), with Helm labels and annotations matching the other Services in the release. I did this with `kubectl apply`, not by changing the Deployment or the frontend config.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The `ad` Service now has an endpoint (`10.244.110.139:8080`).\n- DNS for `ad` resolves from inside the cluster.\n- Frontend \"Name resolution failed\" errors dropped to zero over the last 30 seconds.\n- All pods are Running with no restarts.\n\n**Follow-up:** The Service was removed outside Helm, so a future `helm upgrade` should restore it, but the cause of the deletion is still unknown. Check whether anything in your pipeline or the cluster prunes Services.",
